{
  "_doc": {
    "about": "Dark mode's turning of mail colors, run by web (web/src/lib/dark-mail.spec.ts, shared/src/dark-mail.spec.ts) and Android :core (DarkMailFixturesTest). Colors are [red, green, blue] or [red, green, blue, alpha]; expected colors are CSS as cssColor writes them (#rrggbb, or rgba(…) when not opaque), compared allowing 1 per channel for float differences.",
    "emails": "darkenMessageHtml(html, { palette, colorSchemes, plain }). `unchanged`: the output is the input, exactly. Otherwise each `expect` entry names an element; the last `color` / `background-color` in its output style attribute must be the given color. Every color in the output's <style> sheets is collected: `sheetColors` must all be among them, `sheetAbsent` none. `inline`: the colors in that declaration of the element's output style, in order."
  },
